Objective:
Fix the data "reverting" issue. The app is not showing the latest data from Vercel KV after an update, likely due to Next.js caching.

1. Force Dynamic Rendering:
In app/page.js, app/children/[id]/page.js, and app/finances/page.js, add this line at the very top of the file:

javascript

Copy
export const dynamic = 'force-dynamic';  
export const revalidate = 0;  

    Why: This tells Next.js "Never cache this page. Always fetch fresh data from the database when the user loads it."

2. Update the Store (lib/store.js):
When fetching data from Vercel KV, ensure we aren't using any cached fetch requests (though the KV SDK usually handles this, it's good to be safe).

3. Check the "Save" Logic:
In your Server Actions or API routes (where you save the hours), ensure you are waiting for the KV operation to finish before returning the response.

    Example:

    javascript

    Copy
    // Correct  
    await kv.set('user:default:attendance', newData);  
    return NextResponse.json({ success: true });  

        Incorrect: kv.set(...) (without await) -> This causes the page to reload before the save finishes.

Please apply the force-dynamic fix to all main page files now.